【123†go.sum】  | 【123†go.sum】  |    |\nL237: 【124†integration_test.go】  | 【124†integration_test.go】  |    |\nL238: 【125†version_test.go】  | 【125†version_test.go】  |    |\nL239: [Button: View all files]\nL240: ## Repository files navigation\nL241: \nL242:   *   * 【126†README】\nL243:   * 【126†Code of conduct】\nL244:   * 【126†Contributing】\nL245:   * 【126†Apache-2.0 license】\nL246:   * 【126†Security】\nL247: \nL248: More items\nL249: # `gnark` zk-SNARK library\nL250: \nL251: High-performance zk-SNARKs in Go.\nL252: \nL253: `gnark` provides a high-level API to define circuits, then compile, prove, and verify with production-grade proving systems. It is open-source under Apache 2.0 and uses 【127†`gnark-crypto`】 for field arithmetic and cryptographic primitives.\nL254: \nL255: `gnark` powers 【128†`Linea zk-rollup`†linea.build】. Include your project in 【129†known users】 by opening a PR.\nL256: ## Why `gnark`\nL257: \nL258:   * Circuit development in idiomatic Go\nL259:   * Fast proving and verification backends\nL260:   * Reusable standard gadgets in `std/`\nL261:   * Active security and regression testing culture\nL262: \nL263: ## Useful Links\nL264: \nL265:   * 【130†`gnark` User Documentation†docs.gnark.consensys.net】\nL266:   * 【131†`gnark` Playground†play.gnark.io】\nL267:   * 【132†`gnark` Issues】\nL268:   * 【133†`gnark` Benchmarks†docs.gnark.consensys.net】 🏁\nL269:   * 【134†`gnark-announce`†groups.google.com】 - release and security announcements\nL270: \nL271: ## Quick Start\nL272: ### Requirements\nL273: \nL274:   * Go `1.26+` (module target: `go 1.26.8`)\nL275: \nL276: ### Install\nL277: \nL278:     go get github.com/consensys/gnark@latest\nL279: \nL280: ### Run an example\nL281: \nL282:     go run ./examples/cubic\nL283: \nL284: To design your first circuit, follow the tutorial in 【130†`gnark` User Documentation†docs.gnark.consensys.net】.\nL285: ## Supported Proving Systems and Curves\nL286: \nL287: `gnark` currently supports:\nL288: \nL289:   * Groth16\nL290:   * PLONK\nL291: \nL292: on the following curves:\nL293: \nL294:   * BN254\nL295:   * BLS12-381\nL296:   * BLS12-377\nL297:   * BW6-761\nL298: \nL299: Notes:\nL300: \nL301:   * Solidity verifier export support is curve-dependent (BN254 is the primary target).\nL302:   * Serialized formats are not guaranteed to be stable across versions.\nL303: ## GPU Acceleration (Experimental)\nL304: \nL305: `gnark` includes experimental GPU acceleration through Ingonyama's ICICLE backend for Groth16 on:\nL306: \nL307:   * BN254\nL308:   * BLS12-377\nL309:   * BLS12-381\nL310:   * BW6-761\nL311: \nL312: See 【135†accelerated backend documentation】 and the 【136†ICICLE repository】.\nL313: ## Example Circuit\nL314: The circuit below encodes `x**3 + x + 5 == y`.\nL315: \nL316:     package main\nL317: \nL318:     import (\nL319:     \t\"github.com/consensys/gnark-crypto/ecc\"\nL320:     \t\"github.com/consensys/gnark/backend/groth16\"\nL321:     \t\"github.com/consensys/gnark/frontend\"\nL322:     \t\"github.com/consensys/gnark/frontend/cs/r1cs\"\nL323:     )\nL324: \nL325:     // CubicCircuit defines a simple circuit.\nL326:     // x**3 + x + 5 == y\nL327:     type CubicCircuit struct {\nL328:     \tX frontend.Variable `gnark:\"x\"`\nL329:     \tY frontend.Variable `gnark:\",public\"`\nL330:     }\nL331:     // Define declares the circuit constraints.\nL332:     func (circuit *CubicCircuit) Define(api frontend.API) error {\nL333:     \tx3 := api.Mul(circuit.X, circuit.X, circuit.X)\nL334:     \tapi.AssertIsEqual(circuit.Y, api.Add(x3, circuit.X, 5))\nL335:     \treturn nil\nL336:     }\nL337: \nL338:     func main() {\nL339:     \tvar circuit CubicCircuit\nL340:     \tccs, _ := frontend.Compile(ecc.BN254.ScalarField(), r1cs.NewBuilder, &circuit)\nL341: \nL342:     \tpk, vk, _ := groth16.Setup(ccs)\nL343: \nL344:     \tassignment := CubicCircuit{X: 3, Y: 35}\nL345:     \twitness, _ := frontend.NewWitness(&assignment, ecc.BN254.ScalarField())\nL346:     \tpublicWitness, _ := witness.Public()\nL347: \nL348:     \tproof, _ := groth16.Prove(ccs, pk, witness)\nL349:     \t_ = groth16.Verify(proof, vk, publicWitness)\nL350:     }\nL351: ## Security\nL352: \nL353: `gnark` and 【127†`gnark-crypto`】 have been 【137†extensively audited】, but are provided as-is with no guarantees or warranties. In particular, `gnark` does not guarantee constant-time implementations or side-channel resistance.\nL354: \nL355: Report vulnerabilities via 【119†Security Policy】. Do not open public issues for security reports.\nL356: \nL357: Published advisories are listed 【138†here】.\nL358: ## Testing\nL359: \nL360: CI runs formatting, generated-file, lint, and test checks on pull requests and pushes.\nL361: \nL362: Common local commands:\nL363: \nL364:     go test -short ./...\nL365:     go test -tags=release_checks,solccheck .\nL366:     go test -tags=prover_checks ./test/... ./examples/...\nL367:     go test -run=NONE -fuzz=FuzzIntcomp -fuzztime=30s ./internal/backend/ioutils\nL368:     go generate ./...\nL369: ## Audits\nL370:   * 【139†Kudelski Security - October 2022 - gnark-crypto (contracted by Algorand Foundation)】\nL371:   * 【140†Sigma Prime - May 2024 - gnark-crypto KZG (contracted by Ethereum Foundation)】\nL372:   * 【141†Consensys Diligence - June 2023 - gnark PLONK Solidity verifier†consensys.io】\nL373:   * 【142†LeastAuthority - August 2023 - gnark Groth16 Solidity verifier template (contracted by Worldcoin)†leastauthority.com】\nL374:   * 【143†OpenZeppelin - November 2023 - gnark PLONK Solidity verifier template†blog.openzeppelin.com】\nL375:   * 【144†ZKSecurity.xyz - May 2024 - gnark standard library】\nL376:   * 【145†OpenZeppelin - June 2024 - gnark PLONK prover and verifier†blog.openzeppelin.com】\nL377:   * 【146†LeastAuthority - September 2024 - gnark general and GKR】\nL378:   * 【147†LeastAuthority - November 2024 - Linea zkEVM】\nL379: ## Release Notes\nL380: \nL381: See 【114†CHANGELOG.md】.\nL382: ## Citing\nL383: If you use `gnark` in research, please cite the latest release:\nL384: \nL385:     @software{gnark-v0.16.4,\nL386:       author       = {Gautam Botrel and\nL387:                       Thomas Piellard and\nL388:                       Youssef El Housni and\nL389:                       Ivo Kubjas and\nL390:                       Arya Tabaie and\nL391:                       Yao J. Galteland},\nL392:       title        = {Consensys/gnark: v0.16.4},\nL393:       month        = oct,\nL394:       year         = 2026,\nL395:       publisher    = {Zenodo},\nL396:       version      = {v0.16.4},\nL397:       doi          = {10.5281/zenodo.5819104},\nL398:       url          = {https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.5819104}\nL399:     }\nL400: ## Contributing\nL401: \nL402: See 【116†CONTRIBUTING.md】 and 【115†CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md】.\nL403: \nL404: ## Versioning\nL405: \nL406: `gnark` follows 【148†SemVer†semver.org】. Available versions are in 【149†tags】.\nL407: \nL408: ## License\nL409: \nL410: Licensed under Apache 2.0 (see 【117†LICENSE】).\nL411: \nL412: ## About\nL413: \nL414: gnark is a fast zk-SNARK library that offers a high-level API to design circuits. The library is open source and developed under the Apache 2.0 license\nL415: \nL416: 【71†docs.gnark.consensys.com†docs.gnark.consensys.com】\nL417: ### Topics\nL418: \nL419: 【72†gnark】【73†golang】【74†plonk】【75†r1cs】【76†zk-rollup】【77†zk-snarks】【78†zkevm】【79†zkp】【80†zksnark】\nL420: \nL421: ### Resources\nL422: \nL423: 【81†Readme】\nL424: \nL425: 【82†Apache-2.0 license】\nL426: \nL427: ### Code of conduct\nL428: \nL429: 【83†Code of conduct】\nL430: \nL431: ### Contributing\nL432: \nL433: 【84†Contributing】\nL434: \nL435: ### Security policy\nL436: \nL437: 【85†Security policy】\nL438: \nL439: 【86†Activity】\nL440: \nL441: 【87†Custom properties】\nL442: \nL443: ### Stars\nL444: \nL445: 1.7k stars\nL446: \nL447: ### Watchers\nL448: \nL449: 31 watching\nL450: \nL451: ### Forks\nL452: \nL453: 【88†555 forks】\nL454: \nL455: 【89†Report repository】\nL456: \nL457: ## Releases\nL458: \nL459: ## Used by\nL460: \nL461: ##